Notebook[{
Cell["A Quantum Clock Losing Its Phase", "Subsection",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The problem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " A two-level Ramsey probe accumulates phase under its own Hamiltonian while \
its environment removes the coherence used to read that phase, without \
changing the probe's bare energy populations:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "."], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["z", "TI"]]}], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], "]", "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["\<\
The Hamiltonian turns the clock hand, and the dephasing shortens it. In other \
words, the useful signal and the loss of that signal happen at the same time.\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 " and use"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", 
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
    FractionBox["1", "2"], "{", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["L", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    StyleBox["L", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "}"}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With this convention, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 " damps a qubit coherence at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], "=", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 ". Naming this factor-of-two convention now prevents a common mismatch with \
papers that place a factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 " in front of the dissipator."
}], "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This equation describes a phase or frequency probe relative to the external \
phase used to prepare and read it. A complete frequency standard needs more \
structure: a local oscillator, repeated interrogation cycles, measurement, \
feedback, and a long-time stability metric. Those ingredients are absent here \
and will be identified explicitly when the single-shot calculation reaches \
its boundary. See, for example, the clock protocol of ",
 ButtonBox["Kessler et al.",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.6043"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The equation also determines only the reduced state of the probe. Constant \
probe energy does not by itself determine changes in bath energy, interaction \
energy, or switching work. Pure decoherence can therefore have nontrivial \
thermodynamics even when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"H", "\[Rho]"}], "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 " remains fixed; see ",
 ButtonBox["Popovic, Mitchison, and Goold",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.14216"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],

Cell["\<\
This section uses the density-matrix, Bloch-vector, Lindbladian, \
master-equation, and Bloch-sphere tools already defined in the catalog. Every \
reusable definition below takes its physical parameters as arguments. The \
only numerical physics choices appear together in one editable example \
association, so none of the physics is buried inside a function.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell["\<\
The model and its nearest extensions will be tested in eight complementary \
regimes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["Regime", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
     Cell["Question answered", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"]},
   {Cell["General symbolic", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"], Cell[
    "What happens to an arbitrary physical Bloch vector?", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"]},
   {Cell["Exactly solvable limits", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"], Cell["\<\
What remains when either the Hamiltonian or dephasing is absent?\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"]},
   {Cell["Asymptotic", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"], Cell[
    "Which information survives at long times?", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"]},
   {Cell["Numerical reference", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"], Cell[
    "Does Bloch evolution agree with the full Liouvillian?", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"]},
   {Cell["Failure boundary", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"], Cell[
    "What breaks if a constant dephasing rate is made negative?", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"]},
   {Cell["Joint estimation", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"], Cell["\<\
Can the same state distinguish frequency from dephasing strength?\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"]},
   {Cell["Temporal extension", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"], Cell["\<\
Which conclusions survive when the coherence is not exponential?\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"]},
   {Cell["Spatial extension", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"], Cell["\<\
How do independent and correlated environments change multi-qubit sensing?\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"]}
  },
  GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
  GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {
      Scaled[0.44], 
      Scaled[0.44]}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
  GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.5}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}]], "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],

Cell["\<\
The Commuting Hamiltonian: Energy Stays Put While Phase Moves\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Pure dephasing does not mean that the Hamiltonian is absent. It means that \
the environmental coupling commutes with the system Hamiltonian, so the bath \
cannot move population between energy levels. Here the Hamiltonian and the \
leak are both proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["z", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "scalarExpressionQ", ",", " ", "nonnegativeParameterQ", ",", " ", 
    "blochVectorExpressionQ", ",", "\n", " ", "clockHamiltonian", ",", " ", 
    "dephasingLeak"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"scalarExpressionQ", "[", "expression_", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"!", 
     RowBox[{"ListQ", "[", "expression", "]"}]}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"!", 
     RowBox[{"AssociationQ", "[", "expression", "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"nonnegativeParameterQ", "[", "expression_", "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"scalarExpressionQ", "[", "expression", "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", 
    "   ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"!", 
       RowBox[{"NumericQ", "[", "expression", "]"}]}], " ", "||", " ", 
      RowBox[{"TrueQ", "[", 
       RowBox[{"expression", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochVectorExpressionQ", "[", "expression_", "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MatchQ", "[", 
     RowBox[{"expression", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"_", ",", " ", "_", ",", " ", "_"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&&",
     "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
     RowBox[{"expression", ",", " ", "scalarExpressionQ"}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", 
    RowBox[{"omega_", "?", "scalarExpressionQ"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"omega", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Z", "/", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidClockHamiltonianArguments\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"dephasingLeak", "[", 
    RowBox[{"gamma_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "gamma", "]"}], " ", "Z"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"dephasingLeak", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidDephasingLeakArguments\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that the clock Hamiltonian and the dephasing operator commute:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", "omega", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dephasingLeak", "[", "gamma", "]"}]}], " ", "==", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dephasingLeak", "[", "gamma", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", "omega", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The commuting pair is why this remains ",
 StyleBox["pure", "TI"],
 " dephasing even with the clock switched on. The Hamiltonian changes a \
relative phase, but neither term changes the probabilities of the two energy \
levels."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Read the master equation as Bloch equations for a general state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z", ",", " ", "omega", ",", " ", "gamma", ",",
     " ", "clockRates"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockRates", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"omega_", "?", "scalarExpressionQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gamma_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"rates", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", "omega", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"dephasingLeak", "[", "gamma", "]"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
         "omega", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", 
          "z"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockRates", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidClockRateArguments\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockRates", "[", 
    RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "gamma"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "omega", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", 
        "z"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The output shows that the Hamiltonian couples ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 " into a rotation, dephasing damps both at rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 " remains fixed. The energy populations sit still while the phase-space \
clock hand turns and fades."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],

Cell["\<\
Turn those rates into a drift matrix, then use its matrix exponential to \
evolve any initial Bloch vector:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"clockDrift", ",", " ", "clockBloch"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockDrift", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"omega_", "?", "scalarExpressionQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gamma_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"D", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"clockRates", "[", 
      RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "gamma"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y", ",", " ", "z"}], "}"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockDrift", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidClockDriftArguments\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockBloch", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"r0_", "?", "blochVectorExpressionQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"omega_", "?", "scalarExpressionQ"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"gamma_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"time_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"clockDrift", "[", 
       RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "gamma"}], "]"}], " ", "time"}], "]"}], " ",
     ".", " ", "r0"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockBloch", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidClockBlochArguments\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell["\<\
The function contains no chosen initial state, frequency, rate, or duration. \
It is the general qubit clock under this model.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Find the exact motion from an arbitrary initial Bloch vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "0"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["y", "TI"], "0"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["z", "TI"], "0"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0", ",", " ", "time", ",", " ", 
    "clockSolution"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"clockSolution", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"clockBloch", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      "omega", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
        "x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0", ",", " ", "omega", ",", " ", 
         "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", 
     "&&", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The transverse vector rotates at angular frequency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],
 " and shrinks by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],
 ", while its height ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["z", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 " never changes. A physical initial state also obeys ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "0", "2"], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["y", "TI"], "0", "2"], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "0", "2"], "\[LessEqual]", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 " (its Bloch vector lies inside the unit ball). Verify that the expression \
satisfies both the differential equation and the initial condition:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"D", "[", 
      RowBox[{"clockSolution", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"clockDrift", "[", 
       RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "gamma"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      "clockSolution"}]}], " ", "&&", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"clockSolution", " ", "/.", " ", 
       RowBox[{"time", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ")"}], " ", "==", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0"}], "}"}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0", ",", " ", "omega", ",", " ", 
        "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&",
     "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell["\<\
The evolution must also keep every physical input inside the Bloch ball. \
Verify symbolically that the squared Bloch radius can only decrease:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"clockSolution", " ", ".", " ", "clockSolution"}], " ", "<=", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"y0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"z0", "^", "2"}]}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0", ",", " ", "omega", ",", " ", 
        "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&",
     "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"y0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"z0", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "<=", " ", "1"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell["\<\
This confirms positivity for every qubit input: a valid initial density \
matrix remains inside the Bloch ball. Complete positivity is stronger because \
it also tests the map when the qubit is entangled with an arbitrary ancilla. \
Here complete positivity follows from the positive-rate GKSL form, and the \
explicit phase-flip representation below will make it visible at the channel \
level.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The original Hamiltonian-free example is now one limit rather than the \
whole story. Setting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 " leaves the straight inward slide, while setting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],
 " leaves a perfect clock that rotates forever."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],

Cell["Compute both limits from the same solution:", "Text",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"<|", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<no Hamiltonian\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"clockSolution", " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"omega", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<no dephasing\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"clockSolution", " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"gamma", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "|>"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0", ",", " ", "omega", ",", " ", 
        "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&",
     "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],

Cell["\<\
For any positive dephasing rate, the rotating hand eventually disappears but \
the population imbalance survives. Confirm the long-time state:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
  RowBox[{"clockSolution", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"time", " ", "->", " ", "Infinity"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
        "x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0", ",", " ", "omega", ",", " ", 
         "gamma"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The long-time answer is not a unique steady state. Every diagonal density \
matrix survives because both the identity and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 " belong to the kernel of the Lindbladian. When ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], ">", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["o", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[NotEqual]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 ", these two operators span the fixed space. At the completely switched-off \
corner ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],
 ", the Liouvillian vanishes and every operator is stationary. Verify the two \
universal stationary directions and the four-dimensional exceptional kernel:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"lindbladian", "[", "\n", "      ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", "omega", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"dephasingLeak", "[", "gamma", "]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"id2", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], ")"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"0", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"id2", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "gamma"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], 
     "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Length", "@", 
  RowBox[{"NullSpace", "[", 
   RowBox[{"liouvillian", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"0", " ", "id2"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The exceptional value is ",
 Cell[BoxData["4"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],
 ". Away from that zero-generator corner, the characteristic polynomial \
identifies only the two fixed diagonal directions."
}], "Text",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],

Cell["\<\
The rest of the Liouvillian spectrum tells us how the nonstationary \
directions evolve. Compute its characteristic polynomial:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"liouvillianEigenvalue", ",", " ", "clockLiouvillianPolynomial"}], 
   "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"clockLiouvillianPolynomial", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Factor", "@", 
     RowBox[{"CharacteristicPolynomial", "[", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"liouvillian", "[", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", "omega", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"dephasingLeak", "[", "gamma", "]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         "2"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", "liouvillianEigenvalue"}], "]"}]}], 
    ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "gamma"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], 
      "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The polynomial factors into two zero roots and the pair ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],
 ". At the switched-off corner all four roots coincide at zero. Otherwise the \
zero modes store the identity and population imbalance, while the other pair \
rotates or damps the two coherence directions. This is the first foundational \
point: the probe can lose its phase reference without changing its mean bare \
energy. For positive dephasing, the energy eigenstates are the stable pointer \
states of this model, the simplest instance of environment-induced selection \
discussed by ",
 ButtonBox["Paz and Zurek",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/9811026"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],

Cell["One Editable Experiment: Watching the Clock Hand Fade", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],

Cell["\<\
Before drawing a numerical picture, collect every choice in one place. Change \
this association and every later numerical check and plot will update with it:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "clockExample", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"clockExample", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"frequency", " ", "=", " ", "3"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"dephasingRate", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "5"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"periods", " ", "=", " ", "3"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"samplesPerPeriod", " ", "=", " ", "80"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"probeState", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "plus", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<Frequency\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "frequency"}], ",", "\n", 
       "    ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<DephasingRate\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "dephasingRate"}], ",",
        "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Duration\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"periods", " ", "2", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "frequency"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Samples\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"periods", " ", "samplesPerPeriod"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<ProbeState\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "probeState"}], ",", 
       "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<ReadoutProjector\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "probeState"}]}], 
      "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell["\<\
The duration and number of samples are derived from the requested number of \
clock periods. No later cell repeats these values.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell["\<\
Build the time grid and the Bloch path from that one association:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"clockTimes", ",", " ", "clockPath"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"clockTimes", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"N", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Subdivide", "[", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<Duration\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<Samples\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"clockPath", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"clockBloch", "[", "\n", "     ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
        RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<ProbeState\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
       "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<Frequency\>\"", "]"}], ",", "\n", 
       "     ", 
       RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<DephasingRate\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "clockTimes"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],

Cell["Visualize the quantum clock on the Bloch sphere:", "Text",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"blochPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "clockPath", "}"}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", "\"\<the Hamiltonian turns the clock hand while dephasing shortens it\
\>\""}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],

Cell["\<\
The path winds around the equator while falling inward. Rotation is the \
useful Hamiltonian evolution; radial contraction is the information lost to \
the environment.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],

Cell["\<\
The Bloch calculation and the catalog's Liouvillian solver are independent \
representations of the same state. Compare them over the entire displayed run:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"#1", " ", "-", " ", "#2"}], ",", " ", "\"\<Frobenius\>\""}], 
      "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"blochState", " ", "@@", " ", "#"}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", 
       "/@", " ", "clockPath"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"evolve", "[", "\n", "       ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", 
           RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<Frequency\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",",
           "\n", "       ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"dephasingLeak", "[", 
            RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<DephasingRate\>\"", "]"}], 
            "]"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "       ", 
          RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<ProbeState\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "clockTimes"}]}], "}"}]}],
    "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell["\<\
The two routes agree to numerical rounding: the three-dimensional Bloch drift \
and the four-dimensional Liouvillian describe the same master equation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],

Cell["The Same Evolution as a Computational Phase-Flip Channel", \
"Subsubsection",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For quantum computing, the master equation has an equivalent circuit-level \
meaning. The ideal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],
 " rotation is followed by a stochastic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],
 " error with probability"
}], "Text",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"1", "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{"-", "2", 
        StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}], "2"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],

Cell["\<\
Thus computational-basis populations survive, while coherent phase \
information needed by interference and phase-sensitive gates is progressively \
randomized.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],

Cell["\<\
Build the phase-flip channel and compose it with the ideal clock rotation:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "qubitMatrixQ", ",", " ", "positiveSemidefiniteMatrixQ", ",", "\n", " ", 
    "qubitDensityMatrixQ", ",", " ", "qubitProjectorQ", ",", "\n", " ", 
    "phaseFlipProbability", ",", " ", "phaseFlipChannel", ",", " ", 
    "clockUnitary", ",", " ", "clockChannel"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"qubitMatrixQ", "[", "expression_", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MatrixQ", "[", "expression", "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "expression", "]"}], " ", "===", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"positiveSemidefiniteMatrixQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"matrix_", "?", "MatrixQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions_", " ", ":", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"TrueQ", "@", 
    RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"matrix", " ", "==", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "matrix", "]"}]}], " ", "&&", "\n",
        "     ", 
       RowBox[{"And", " ", "@@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
         RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "       ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
             RowBox[{"subset", ",", "\n", "         ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
                RowBox[{"matrix", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", 
                  RowBox[{"subset", ",", " ", "subset"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}],
                " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}], " ", "/@", "\n", "        ", 
            RowBox[{"Subsets", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
               RowBox[{"Length", "[", "matrix", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", "order", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "       ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"order", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Length", "[", "matrix", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], ",",
       "\n", "    ", "assumptions"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"positiveSemidefiniteMatrixQ", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=",
    " ", "False"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"qubitDensityMatrixQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"matrix_", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions_", " ", ":", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"qubitMatrixQ", "[", "matrix", "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"positiveSemidefiniteMatrixQ", "[", 
     RowBox[{"matrix", ",", " ", "assumptions"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", 
    "   ", 
    RowBox[{"TrueQ", "@", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "matrix", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
       "assumptions"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"qubitProjectorQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"matrix_", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions_", " ", ":", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"qubitMatrixQ", "[", "matrix", "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"TrueQ", "@", 
     RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "     ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"matrix", " ", "==", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "matrix", "]"}]}], " ", "&&", 
        "\n", "      ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"matrix", " ", ".", " ", "matrix"}], " ", "==", " ", 
         "matrix"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", "assumptions"}], "]"}]}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"phaseFlipProbability", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gamma_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"time_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "gamma", " ", "time"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
    "2"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"phaseFlipProbability", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidPhaseFlipProbabilityArguments\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"phaseFlipChannel", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"rho_", "?", "qubitMatrixQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gamma_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"time_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"phaseFlipProbability", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "p"}], ")"}], " ", "rho"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"p", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Z", " ", ".", " ", "rho", " ", ".", " ", "Z"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}],
   ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"phaseFlipChannel", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidPhaseFlipChannelArguments\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockUnitary", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"omega_", "?", "scalarExpressionQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"time_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", "omega", "]"}], " ", "time"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockUnitary", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidClockUnitaryArguments\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockChannel", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"rho_", "?", "qubitMatrixQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"omega_", "?", "scalarExpressionQ"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"gamma_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"time_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"unitary", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"clockUnitary", "[", 
        RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"unitary", " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"phaseFlipChannel", "[", 
       RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}], " ", ".", 
      "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "unitary", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockChannel", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidClockChannelArguments\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->1621535814,ExpressionUUID->"52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],

Cell["\<\
Verify first that the error probability stays physical, then verify the \
channel against the general Bloch solution:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"phaseFlipProbability", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}], " ", "<=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], " ", "&&", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"clockChannel", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"blochState", "[", 
        RowBox[{"x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       "omega", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}], " ", "==", "\n",
      "   ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"blochState", " ", "@@", " ", "clockSolution"}], ")"}]}]}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0", ",", " ", "omega", ",", " ", 
        "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&",
     "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"y0", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"z0", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "<=", " ", "1"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->105329933,ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell["\<\
This is the computing version of pure dephasing: a classical bit stored in \
the energy basis is stable, but a quantum superposition accumulates \
phase-flip error.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1234416869,ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell["\<\
The channel comparison uses several physical invariants. Check them together \
for a general real Bloch state:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->240380995,ExpressionUUID->"36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"assumptions", " ", "=", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
         "x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0", ",", " ", "omega", ",", " ", 
          "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ",
       "&&", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Map", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
       RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "assumptions"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<Hamiltonian is Hermitian\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", "omega", "]"}], " ", "==", "\n", 
         "      ", 
         RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", 
          RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", "omega", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
       "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<clock rotation is unitary\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "     ", 
        
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", 
           RowBox[{"clockUnitary", "[", 
            RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", "\n",
           "       ", 
          RowBox[{"clockUnitary", "[", 
           RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}]}], " ", "==", " ", 
         "id2"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<generator preserves trace\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "     ", 
        
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
          RowBox[{"lindbladian", "[", "\n", "        ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", "omega", "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"dephasingLeak", "[", "gamma", "]"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
            "        ", 
            RowBox[{"blochState", "[", 
             RowBox[{"x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
          "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<bare energy is conserved\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", "omega", "]"}], " ", ".", "\n", 
           "        ", 
           RowBox[{"lindbladian", "[", "\n", "         ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"clockHamiltonian", "[", "omega", "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"dephasingLeak", "[", "gamma", "]"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
             "         ", 
             RowBox[{"blochState", "[", 
              RowBox[{"x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0"}], "]"}]}], 
            "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->1771870337,ExpressionUUID->"6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All four entries are ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 ". The trace remains one, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],
 "-energy expectation remains fixed, and the coherent part is a genuine \
unitary rotation."
}], "Text",
 CellID->305160771,ExpressionUUID->"06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],

Cell["Ramsey Interference: Turning the Invisible Phase into Data", \
"Subsubsection",
 CellID->1896945989,ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A phase has no operational meaning until an interferometer converts it into \
a probability. Prepare ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 ", let the clock evolve, and measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 " again. This is a Ramsey experiment (a phase-accumulation interval closed \
by a second ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 " pulse), written directly as a projector probability."
}], "Text",
 CellID->653417278,ExpressionUUID->"65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],

Cell["\<\
Define the Ramsey probability from the state produced by the general Bloch \
evolution:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1067269536,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "ramseyProbability", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ramseyProbability", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
    "probeState_", ",", " ", "readoutProjector_", ",", " ", "omega_", ",", 
     " ", "gamma_", ",", " ", "time_", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions_", " ", ":", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Which", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"!", 
      RowBox[{"qubitDensityMatrixQ", "[", 
       RowBox[{"probeState", ",", " ", "assumptions"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidRamseyProbeState\>\"", ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<ProbeState\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", "probeState", "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"!", 
      RowBox[{"qubitProjectorQ", "[", 
       RowBox[{"readoutProjector", ",", " ", "assumptions"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidRamseyReadoutProjector\>\"", ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<ReadoutProjector\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", "readoutProjector", "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], 
      "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"!", 
       RowBox[{"scalarExpressionQ", "[", "omega", "]"}]}], " ", "||", "\n", 
      "    ", 
      RowBox[{"!", 
       RowBox[{"nonnegativeParameterQ", "[", "gamma", "]"}]}], " ", "||", 
      "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"!", 
       RowBox[{"nonnegativeParameterQ", "[", "time", "]"}]}], " ", "||", "\n",
       "    ", 
      RowBox[{"!", 
       RowBox[{"scalarExpressionQ", "[", "assumptions", "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidRamseyParameters\>\"", ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<Parameters\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], 
           "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Assumptions\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", "assumptions", "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}], 
     ",", "\n", "   ", "True", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
      RowBox[{"readoutProjector", " ", ".", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"blochState", " ", "@@", "\n", "       ", 
         RowBox[{"clockBloch", "[", "\n", "        ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "probeState", "]"}], ",", " ", "omega",
            ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ramseyProbability", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidRamseyProbabilityArguments\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->49659130,ExpressionUUID->"78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],

Cell["Find the Ramsey fringe in closed form:", "Text",
 CellID->464508221,ExpressionUUID->"08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ramseyProbability", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<ProbeState\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<ReadoutProjector\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", "omega", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", 
      " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->1361313038,ExpressionUUID->"1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The oscillation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "t"}], "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],
 " carries the frequency, and the envelope ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],
 " erases its visibility. In other words, waiting longer writes more signal \
phase but also makes that phase harder to read."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1907680634,ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell["\<\
Compare the ideal and dephasing-limited Ramsey fringes using the same \
experiment association:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->483148123,ExpressionUUID->"112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"frequency", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<Frequency\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"dephasingRate", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<DephasingRate\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"duration", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<Duration\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Plot", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Evaluate", "@", 
      RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ramseyProbability", "[", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<ProbeState\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          
          RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<ReadoutProjector\>\"", "]"}], ",",
           "\n", "     ", "frequency", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "time"}], 
         "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"ramseyProbability", "[", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<ProbeState\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          
          RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<ReadoutProjector\>\"", "]"}], ",",
           "\n", "     ", "frequency", ",", " ", "dephasingRate", ",", " ", 
          "time"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"time", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "duration"}], "}"}], ",", "\n",
      "  ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
         RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<ideal clock\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<dephasing-limited clock\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "540"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<interrogation time\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<Ramsey probability\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
     "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<dephasing erases Ramsey-fringe visibility\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->1195452142,ExpressionUUID->"6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This picture is what ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], "=", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 " means in a clock or sensor: not an abstract shrinking vector, but a \
disappearing experimental fringe."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1521685512,ExpressionUUID->"29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],

Cell["The Best Time to Measure: More Phase Versus Less Contrast", \
"Subsubsection",
 CellID->97201263,ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How long should the clock run before we read it? The answer follows from \
the quantum Fisher information (the maximum frequency information available \
in the state). For a qubit with Bloch vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"],
    FontWeight->"Bold"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],
 ","
}], "Text",
 CellID->878831761,ExpressionUUID->"62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
          StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], 
         StyleBox[
          StyleBox["r", "TI"],
          FontWeight->"Bold"]}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "+", 
    FractionBox[
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox[
         StyleBox["r", "TI"],
         FontWeight->"Bold"], "\[CenterDot]", 
        SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
         StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], 
        StyleBox[
         StyleBox["r", "TI"],
         FontWeight->"Bold"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], 
     RowBox[{"1", "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
         {
          StyleBox[
           StyleBox["r", "TI"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"]}
        },
        GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
        GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1048559713,ExpressionUUID->"7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "whenever the state is mixed. For a parameterized family that remains pure, \
the value is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
        StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox[
        StyleBox["r", "TI"],
        FontWeight->"Bold"]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],
 ". At a rank-changing boundary the quantum Fisher information need not be \
continuous, so the family domain must be stated rather than guessed."
}], "Text",
 CellID->300048012,ExpressionUUID->"657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build that expression as a reusable function of a Bloch vector, a \
parameter, an explicit family domain, and optional assumptions. It verifies \
that the vector is real and lies in the declared domain. A pure family must \
remain on the Bloch sphere and have a tangent derivative; otherwise the \
function returns a ",
 Cell[BoxData["Failure"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 " instead of silently choosing a boundary formula:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1962937852,ExpressionUUID->"7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "blochFisherInformation", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochFisherInformation", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"r_", "?", "blochVectorExpressionQ"}], ",", " ", 
     "parameter_Symbol", ",", " ", "domain_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   
   RowBox[{"blochFisherInformation", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "r", ",", " ", "parameter", ",", " ", "domain", ",", " ", "True"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochFisherInformation", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"r_", "?", "blochVectorExpressionQ"}], ",", " ", 
     "parameter_Symbol", ",", " ", "\"\<Mixed\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions_", "?", "scalarExpressionQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"dr", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"D", "[", 
         RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "parameter"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"radius2", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"r", " ", ".", " ", "r"}], ",", " ", "assumptions"}], 
         "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"If", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"TrueQ", "@", 
        RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
            RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
           RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "radius2", " ", "<", " ", "1"}]}], ",",
           " ", "assumptions"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"dr", " ", ".", " ", "dr"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"r", " ", ".", " ", "dr"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "radius2"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
         "assumptions"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<UnverifiedMixedBlochFamily\>\"", ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"<|", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\"\<BlochVector\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "r"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<Assumptions\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "assumptions"}]}], 
          "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochFisherInformation", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"r_", "?", "blochVectorExpressionQ"}], ",", " ", 
     "parameter_Symbol", ",", " ", "\"\<Pure\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions_", "?", "scalarExpressionQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"dr", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"D", "[", 
         RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "parameter"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"radius2", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"r", " ", ".", " ", "r"}], ",", " ", "assumptions"}], 
         "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"If", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"TrueQ", "@", 
        RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
            RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
           RowBox[{"radius2", " ", "==", " ", "1"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"r", " ", ".", " ", "dr"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}]}], ",", 
          " ", "assumptions"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"dr", " ", ".", " ", "dr"}], ",", " ", "assumptions"}], 
        "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<UnverifiedPureBlochFamily\>\"", ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"<|", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\"\<BlochVector\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "r"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<Assumptions\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "assumptions"}]}], 
          "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochFisherInformation", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"r_", "?", "blochVectorExpressionQ"}], ",", " ", 
     "parameter_Symbol", ",", " ", "domain_", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions_", "?", "scalarExpressionQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<UnknownBlochFamilyDomain\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<Domain\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "domain"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<AllowedDomains\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Mixed\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Pure\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
      "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochFisherInformation", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidBlochFisherArguments\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->588230824,ExpressionUUID->"585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],

Cell["\<\
Exercise the declared boundaries instead of leaving the failure behavior \
implicit:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2099309037,ExpressionUUID->"1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<pure vector declared mixed\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"blochFisherInformation", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "omega", 
      ",", " ", "\"\<Mixed\>\""}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<mixed vector declared pure\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"blochFisherInformation", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
      " ", "omega", ",", " ", "\"\<Pure\>\""}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<unknown family domain\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"blochFisherInformation", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
      " ", "omega", ",", " ", "\"\<Boundary\>\""}], "]"}]}]}], 
  "|>"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:= ",
 CellID->512383039,ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each entry is a named ",
 Cell[BoxData["Failure"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],
 ", so an invalid rank assumption cannot silently produce a \
Fisher-information value."
}], "Text",
 CellID->273308241,ExpressionUUID->"7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],

Cell["\<\
Exercise the successful pure-family branch on the noiseless equatorial clock:\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1809098798,ExpressionUUID->"594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"blochFisherInformation", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"omega", " ", "time"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
      RowBox[{"omega", " ", "time"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ",
    "omega", ",", " ", "\"\<Pure\>\"", ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}],
     " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:= ",
 CellID->156430199,ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The pure-state information is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],
 ", as expected for an undamped phase rotation."
}], "Text",
 CellID->724760089,ExpressionUUID->"48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],

Cell["\<\
Apply it to the dephasing clock, keeping the derivation symbolic:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->168408080,ExpressionUUID->"539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"clockVector", ",", " ", "clockQFI"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"clockVector", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"clockBloch", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
      RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<ProbeState\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
     " ", "omega", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"clockQFI", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", 
         " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{"time", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"blochFisherInformation", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "clockVector", ",", " ", "omega", ",", " ", "\"\<Mixed\>\"", ",", " ", 
      "assumptions"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:= ",
 CellID->811283638,ExpressionUUID->"7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "4", 
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],
 ": the ideal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],
 " gain is multiplied by the square of the surviving contrast. Confirm that \
the noiseless limit returns the ideal clock:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->207978548,ExpressionUUID->"289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
     RowBox[{"clockQFI", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gamma", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"time", "^", "2"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{"time", ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:= ",
 CellID->437474228,ExpressionUUID->"12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],

Cell["\<\
Positive dephasing eventually removes all frequency information from this \
equatorial probe:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->874582697,ExpressionUUID->"7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
  RowBox[{"clockQFI", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"time", " ", "->", " ", "Infinity"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gamma", ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:= ",
 CellID->11631581,ExpressionUUID->"2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],

Cell["\<\
The limit is zero. Population imbalance may survive forever, but it does not \
encode the rotation frequency in this model.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1933762060,ExpressionUUID->"362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same output state contains information about the noise strength. For \
parameters ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],
 ", the mixed-state Bloch formula generalizes to the matrix"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1055776787,ExpressionUUID->"107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]], "=", 
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"],
     FontWeight->"Bold"], "\[CenterDot]", 
    SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox[
     StyleBox["r", "TI"],
     FontWeight->"Bold"], "+", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox[
        StyleBox["r", "TI"],
        FontWeight->"Bold"], "\[CenterDot]", 
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox[
        StyleBox["r", "TI"],
        FontWeight->"Bold"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox[
        StyleBox["r", "TI"],
        FontWeight->"Bold"], "\[CenterDot]", 
       SubscriptBox["\[PartialD]", 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
       StyleBox[
        StyleBox["r", "TI"],
        FontWeight->"Bold"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     RowBox[{"1", "-", 
      SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
         {
          StyleBox[
           StyleBox["r", "TI"],
           FontWeight->"Bold"]}
        },
        GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
        GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}]]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1859711813,ExpressionUUID->"6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],

Cell["\<\
In other words, the diagonal entries quantify separate sensitivities and the \
off-diagonal entries reveal local statistical coupling between parameters.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1348896709,ExpressionUUID->"49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],

Cell["\<\
Build the mixed-state quantum Fisher information matrix from the same Bloch \
vector:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1427211115,ExpressionUUID->"2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "blochFisherInformationMatrix", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochFisherInformationMatrix", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"r_", "?", "blochVectorExpressionQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"parameters", " ", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "__Symbol", "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"blochFisherInformationMatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "parameters", ",", " ", "True"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochFisherInformationMatrix", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"r_", "?", "blochVectorExpressionQ"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"parameters", " ", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "__Symbol", "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions_", "?", "scalarExpressionQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"derivatives", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"D", "[", 
           RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         "parameters"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"radius2", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"r", " ", ".", " ", "r"}], ",", " ", "assumptions"}], 
         "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"If", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"TrueQ", "@", 
        RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
            RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
           RowBox[{"0", " ", "<=", " ", "radius2", " ", "<", " ", "1"}]}], ",",
           " ", "assumptions"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Outer", "[", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"leftDerivative", ",", " ", "rightDerivative"}], "}"}], 
             ",", "\n", "       ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"leftDerivative", " ", ".", " ", "rightDerivative"}], 
              " ", "+", "\n", "        ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"r", " ", ".", " ", "leftDerivative"}], ")"}], " ", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{"r", " ", ".", " ", "rightDerivative"}], ")"}], "/", 
                
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "radius2"}], ")"}]}]}]}]}], 
            "]"}], ",", "\n", "      ", "derivatives", ",", " ", 
           "derivatives", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         "assumptions"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<UnverifiedMixedBlochFamily\>\"", ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"<|", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\"\<BlochVector\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "r"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<Assumptions\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "assumptions"}]}], 
          "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"blochFisherInformationMatrix", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=",
    "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidBlochFisherMatrixArguments\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:= ",
 CellID->2099805207,ExpressionUUID->"0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the joint information for frequency and dephasing strength:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1402006442,ExpressionUUID->"52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "clockJointQFI", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"clockJointQFI", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", 
         " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{"time", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"blochFisherInformationMatrix", "[", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"clockVector", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "gamma"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "assumptions"}],
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[30]:= ",
 CellID->1901179466,ExpressionUUID->"1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],

Cell["Verify its closed form:", "Text",
 CellID->210724908,ExpressionUUID->"062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"clockJointQFI", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"time", "^", "2"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "4"}], " ", "gamma", " ", "time"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ",
         "0"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"time", "^", "2"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
             RowBox[{"4", " ", "gamma", " ", "time"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
            "1"}], ")"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", 
      " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"time", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[31]:= ",
 CellID->1992790374,ExpressionUUID->"1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],

Cell["\<\
The zero cross term means that frequency moves the Bloch vector tangentially \
while dephasing pulls it radially inward. It does not by itself prove that \
one measurement simultaneously saturates both single-parameter bounds; \
measurement compatibility is the next multiparameter question.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->292747604,ExpressionUUID->"6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],

Cell["\<\
The dephasing entry is also nonregular at the noiseless boundary. Extract its \
leading divergence:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1553818268,ExpressionUUID->"612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gamma", " ", 
      RowBox[{"clockJointQFI", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gamma", " ", "->", " ", "0"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Direction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<FromAbove\>\""}]}], "]"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{"time", ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"time", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:= ",
 CellID->1870754514,ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The limit is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", "\[Gamma]"}], "TI"]], "\[Tilde]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],
 " as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", 
   SuperscriptBox["0", "+"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],
 ". This is a rank-changing boundary, not infinite regular precision at an \
interior point. A complete joint-estimation study must therefore state a \
neighborhood or prior for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],
 " and test symmetric-logarithmic-derivative compatibility or the Holevo \
bound for the allowed measurement model."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1358728755,ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Suppose the total available laboratory time is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],
 ". Ignoring preparation, readout, and dead-time overhead, an interrogation \
lasting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],
 " can be repeated ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],
 " times. This continuous repetition count is an asymptotic resource model, \
not yet a complete laboratory schedule. Within it, the information is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "/", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],
 ". Find its stationary point rather than inserting an answer:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->935019337,ExpressionUUID->"106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "totalTime", ",", " ", "clockTotalQFI", ",", " ", "clockOptimalTime"}], 
   "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"clockTotalQFI", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"totalTime", " ", 
      RowBox[{"clockQFI", "/", "time"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"totalTime", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",",
         " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"totalTime", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"time", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"clockOptimalTime", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"time", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"First", "@", 
       RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"D", "[", 
           RowBox[{"clockTotalQFI", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ",
           "0"}], ",", " ", "time", ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n",
      "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"totalTime", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", "clockOptimalTime"}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[33]:= ",
 CellID->642744358,ExpressionUUID->"7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The stationary point is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "*"], "=", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],
 ". Waiting less wastes available phase accumulation; waiting more throws \
away too much contrast. Verify that the stationary point is a maximum:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1478372881,ExpressionUUID->"6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"D", "[", 
       RowBox[{"clockTotalQFI", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"time", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"time", " ", "->", " ", "clockOptimalTime"}]}], ")"}], " ", "<",
     " ", "0"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"totalTime", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[34]:= ",
 CellID->124263719,ExpressionUUID->"4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An interrogation cannot last longer than the available laboratory time. \
Impose the physical domain ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", "<", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[LessEqual]", 
   StyleBox["T", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1310926461,ExpressionUUID->"2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "clockFeasibleOptimalTime", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"clockFeasibleOptimalTime", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
     RowBox[{"totalTime", ",", " ", "clockOptimalTime"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"totalTime", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[35]:= ",
 CellID->1124211690,ExpressionUUID->"3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Therefore the feasible optimum is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["min",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "{", 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"4", 
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],
 ". Integer shot counts, dead time, state-preparation noise, and readout \
noise would modify this resource model rather than the one-shot QFI."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1335749844,ExpressionUUID->"6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],

Cell["\<\
Visualize the information gained per unit laboratory time and mark the \
optimum derived above:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->793802945,ExpressionUUID->"055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"dephasingRate", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<DephasingRate\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"duration", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<Duration\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{"optimum", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"clockOptimalTime", " ", "/.", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gamma", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<DephasingRate\>\"", "]"}]}]}]}]}], 
    "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Plot", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"clockTotalQFI", "/", "totalTime"}], ")"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gamma", " ", "->", " ", "dephasingRate"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n",
      "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"time", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "duration"}], "}"}], ",", "\n",
      "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "520"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<interrogation time\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<Fisher information per total time\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
     "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
     "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<there is a best time to read a dephasing-limited clock\>\""}],
      ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Red", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"InfiniteLine", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"optimum", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"optimum", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
       "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[36]:= ",
 CellID->631769182,ExpressionUUID->"2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],

Cell["\<\
The simple master equation has now answered a narrow engineering question: it \
tells an ideal Ramsey probe when to stop accumulating phase and measure.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1873681340,ExpressionUUID->"201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],

Cell["A Ramsey Probe Is Not Yet a Frequency Standard", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->1468251080,ExpressionUUID->"7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The probability above estimates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],
 " relative to the phase reference that prepares and reads the qubit. A \
working clock must repeatedly compare that atomic phase with a noisy local \
oscillator and use the outcomes to steer the oscillator. In other words, \
state QFI quantifies information inside one interrogation, while long-term \
clock performance depends on the entire estimation and feedback loop."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1989234463,ExpressionUUID->"160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This distinction changes both the objective and the optimum. Real clock \
studies optimize quantities such as Allan variance in the presence of \
local-oscillator noise, finite cycle time, phase ambiguity, and feedback. \
Entanglement can still help in that broader task, but the result no longer \
follows from the reduced master equation alone; see ",
 ButtonBox["Andre, Sorensen, and Lukin",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0401130"], None}],
 " and ",
 ButtonBox["Kessler et al.",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.6043"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1607696641,ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell["Entanglement Meets Dephasing: Faster Phase, Faster Loss", \
"Subsubsection",
 CellID->1817342824,ExpressionUUID->"3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Can ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],
 " entangled clocks beat ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],
 " independent clocks? A GHZ state accumulates phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],
 " times faster, but independent dephasing multiplies its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],
 " single-qubit coherences. Compute the one-qubit visibility from the Bloch \
solution rather than entering its decay law by hand:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->530774412,ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"transverseLength", ",", " ", "singleClockVisibility"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"transverseLength", "[", 
    RowBox[{"r", " ", ":", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"_", ",", " ", "_", ",", " ", "_"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Take", "[", 
      RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Take", "[", 
      RowBox[{"r", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"singleClockVisibility", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"transverseLength", "[", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"clockBloch", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
        RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<ProbeState\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
       " ", "0", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
    "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], 
      "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[37]:= ",
 CellID->599957810,ExpressionUUID->"4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For independent environments, the GHZ visibility is the product of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],
 " copies of this number. Its effective logical Bloch vector therefore \
rotates through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"n", "\[Omega]", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],
 " with transverse length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"singleClockVisibility", "^", "n"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1899946997,ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell["\<\
Construct that logical Bloch vector and compute its frequency information:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1051619128,ExpressionUUID->"5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "ghzClockVector", ",", " ", "ghzQFI"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ghzClockVector", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"singleClockVisibility", "^", "n"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
       RowBox[{"n", " ", "omega", " ", "time"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"singleClockVisibility", "^", "n"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"n", " ", "omega", " ", "time"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], 
    "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ghzQFI", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", 
         " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
        RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "PositiveIntegers"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{"time", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"blochFisherInformation", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "ghzClockVector", ",", " ", "omega", ",", " ", "\"\<Mixed\>\"", ",", " ",
       "assumptions"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[38]:= ",
 CellID->1921351195,ExpressionUUID->"128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],
 " is the faster signal, while the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 " in the exponential is the faster loss. The following comparison assumes \
equal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],
 "-probe resources, independent identical local time-homogeneous Markovian \
dephasing, parallel interrogation, negligible preparation and readout \
overhead, optimal measurements, and enough total laboratory time to reach \
both stationary interrogation times. Within that regime, optimize the \
independent and GHZ strategies over the same total laboratory time."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1207491739,ExpressionUUID->"63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],

Cell["\<\
Compute both total informations and derive their optimal interrogation times:\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->216741342,ExpressionUUID->"387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "productTotalQFI", ",", " ", "ghzTotalQFI", ",", " ", "ghzOptimalTime"}], 
   "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"productTotalQFI", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"totalTime", " ", "n", " ", 
      RowBox[{"clockQFI", "/", "time"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"totalTime", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",",
         " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "PositiveIntegers"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"totalTime", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"time", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ghzTotalQFI", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"totalTime", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ghzQFI", "/", "time"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"totalTime", ",", " ", "gamma", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",",
         " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "PositiveIntegers"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"totalTime", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"time", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ghzOptimalTime", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"time", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"First", "@", 
       RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"D", "[", 
           RowBox[{"ghzTotalQFI", ",", " ", "time"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
          "0"}], ",", " ", "time", ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
     "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
       RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "PositiveIntegers"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"totalTime", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<independent clocks\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "clockOptimalTime"}],
    ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<GHZ clock\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "ghzOptimalTime"}]}], 
  "|>"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[39]:= ",
 CellID->2096934290,ExpressionUUID->"3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The GHZ clock must be read ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 " times sooner. Now compare the two optimized total informations:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1367217003,ExpressionUUID->"1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"productTotalQFI", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"time", " ", "->", " ", "clockOptimalTime"}]}], ")"}], " ", "==",
     "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"ghzTotalQFI", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"time", " ", "->", " ", "ghzOptimalTime"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "PositiveIntegers"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"totalTime", " ", ">=", " ", "clockOptimalTime"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[40]:= ",
 CellID->1372538143,ExpressionUUID->"6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this long-budget regime, independent Markovian dephasing cancels the GHZ \
state's scaling advantage: the entangled state is more responsive and equally \
more fragile. If ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "<", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],
 ", one or both stationary times are infeasible and the boundary values must \
be compared instead; the equality need not hold. This many-repeat asymptotic \
equivalence is the central frequency-standard result of ",
 ButtonBox["Huelga et al.",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/9707014"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->485911656,ExpressionUUID->"6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],

Cell["\<\
The equality compares product probes with maximally entangled GHZ probes; it \
is not a theorem that every entangled state is useless. Partially entangled \
symmetric states can retain a constant-factor improvement even when the \
asymptotic scaling returns to the standard quantum limit. More importantly, \
the scaling conclusion changes when the short-time decay is not a semigroup \
or when different probes see correlated noise. The temporal extension will be \
computed below; first let us expose the spatial assumption.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->181917407,ExpressionUUID->"74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],

Cell["Spatial Correlations: Noise Geometry Changes the Answer", \
"Subsubsection",
 CellID->1906087345,ExpressionUUID->"735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The calculation above assumes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],
 " independent environments. A general Markovian pure-dephasing model instead \
contains a positive semidefinite correlation matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->354048744,ExpressionUUID->"045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
     StyleBox["C", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"]}],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]], "(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "-", 
      FractionBox["1", "2"], "{", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "}"}]}], ")"}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], "\[SucceedsEqual]", 
    RowBox[{"0", "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->786710823,ExpressionUUID->"73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Diagonal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],
 " gives independent noise; an all-ones ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],
 " gives collective noise generated by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "1"], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "2"], "+", "\[CenterEllipsis]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],
 ". In other words, the matrix records which probes hear the same fluctuating \
field."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1859374462,ExpressionUUID->"15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],

Cell["\<\
Define the correlated generator for a supplied list of Hermitian dephasing \
operators:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->544914423,ExpressionUUID->"27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "correlatedDephasingGenerator", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"correlatedDephasingGenerator", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
    "state_", ",", " ", "correlationMatrix_", ",", " ", "operators_", ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions_", " ", ":", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Which", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"!", 
       RowBox[{"MatrixQ", "[", "state", "]"}]}], " ", "||", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "state", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "=!=", " ", 
       "2"}], " ", "||", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"!", 
       RowBox[{"SameQ", " ", "@@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "state", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidStateMatrix\>\"", ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<StateDimensions\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "state", "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"!", 
       RowBox[{"ListQ", "[", "operators", "]"}]}], " ", "||", " ", 
      RowBox[{"operators", " ", "===", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], " ", "||", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"!", 
       RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
        RowBox[{"operators", ",", " ", "MatrixQ"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidDephasingOperators\>\"", ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Operators\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", "operators", "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"!", 
       RowBox[{"MatrixQ", "[", "correlationMatrix", "]"}]}], " ", "||", "\n", 
      "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "correlationMatrix", "]"}], " ", "=!=", 
       "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Length", "[", "operators", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Length", "[", "operators", "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidCorrelationDimensions\>\"", ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<CorrelationDimensions\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "correlationMatrix", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
         "      ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<OperatorCount\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Length", "[", "operators", "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"!", 
      RowBox[{"SameQ", " ", "@@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"Dimensions", " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
          RowBox[{"operators", ",", " ", "state"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<IncompatibleOperatorDimensions\>\"", ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<StateAndOperatorDimensions\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", 
         "       ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"Dimensions", " ", "/@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
            RowBox[{"operators", ",", " ", "state"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], 
        "|>"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"!", 
      RowBox[{"TrueQ", "@", 
       RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"And", " ", "@@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"#", " ", "==", " ", 
              RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}]}], " ", "&"}], 
            " ", "/@", " ", "operators"}], ")"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         "assumptions"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<UnverifiedHermitianDephasingOperators\>\"", ",", "\n", 
       "    ", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Assumptions\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "assumptions"}], 
        "|>"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"!", 
      RowBox[{"TrueQ", "@", 
       RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "      ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"correlationMatrix", " ", "==", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "correlationMatrix", "]"}]}], 
          " ", "&&", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"And", " ", "@@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Flatten", "@", 
            RowBox[{"Table", "[", "\n", "        ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
                RowBox[{"subset", ",", "\n", "          ", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"correlationMatrix", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"subset", ",", " ", "subset"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
                   "]"}], " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}], " ", "/@", "\n", 
               "         ", 
               RowBox[{"Subsets", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"Length", "[", "correlationMatrix", "]"}], "]"}], ",",
                  " ", 
                 RowBox[{"{", "order", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
              "        ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"order", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Length", "[", "correlationMatrix", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
             "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", "assumptions"}], "]"}]}]}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<UnverifiedPhysicalCorrelationMatrix\>\"", ",", "\n", 
       "    ", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<CorrelationMatrix\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
          "correlationMatrix"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Assumptions\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "assumptions"}]}], 
        "|>"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", "True", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Total", "@", 
      RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"coefficient", ",", " ", "pair"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
          "      ", 
          RowBox[{"With", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"leftOperator", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"First", "[", "pair", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "        ", 
              RowBox[{"rightOperator", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Last", "[", "pair", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
            "       ", 
            RowBox[{"coefficient", " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", "\n", "         ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
               "leftOperator", " ", ".", " ", "state", " ", ".", " ", 
                "rightOperator"}], " ", "-", "\n", "          ", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{
                  "rightOperator", " ", ".", " ", "leftOperator", " ", ".", 
                   " ", "state"}], " ", "+", "\n", "             ", 
                  RowBox[{
                  "state", " ", ".", " ", "rightOperator", " ", ".", " ", 
                   "leftOperator"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
           "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", "correlationMatrix", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
           RowBox[{"operators", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[41]:= ",
 CellID->1088734259,ExpressionUUID->"285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build the two-qubit GHZ state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"00"},
      "Ket"], "+", 
     TemplateBox[{"11"},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],
 " and the decoherence-free candidate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"01"},
      "Ket"], "+", 
     TemplateBox[{"10"},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->476175344,ExpressionUUID->"1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "twoQubitBasis", ",", " ", "zOne", ",", " ", "zTwo", ",", " ", 
    "ghzTwoQubitState", ",", " ", "dfsTwoQubitState", ",", "\n", " ", 
    "independentCorrelation", ",", " ", "collectiveCorrelation"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"twoQubitBasis", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "4", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"zOne", ",", " ", "zTwo"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Z", ",", " ", "id2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
      RowBox[{"id2", ",", " ", "Z"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ghzTwoQubitState", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"twoQubitBasis", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"twoQubitBasis", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"dfsTwoQubitState", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"twoQubitBasis", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"twoQubitBasis", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
     RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "2", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"independentCorrelation", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"gamma", " ", 
    RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"collectiveCorrelation", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"gamma", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[42]:= ",
 CellID->201272189,ExpressionUUID->"10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],

Cell["\<\
Compare the squared Frobenius norm of the generator on both states under \
independent and collective noise:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->320292756,ExpressionUUID->"457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "dephasingActivities", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"dephasingActivities", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gamma", ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
    RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"generators", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"correlatedDephasingGenerator", "[", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{
           "ghzTwoQubitState", ",", " ", "independentCorrelation", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"zOne", ",", " ", "zTwo"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            "assumptions"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"correlatedDephasingGenerator", "[", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{
           "dfsTwoQubitState", ",", " ", "independentCorrelation", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"zOne", ",", " ", "zTwo"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            "assumptions"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"correlatedDephasingGenerator", "[", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{
           "ghzTwoQubitState", ",", " ", "collectiveCorrelation", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"zOne", ",", " ", "zTwo"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            "assumptions"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
          RowBox[{"correlatedDephasingGenerator", "[", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{
           "dfsTwoQubitState", ",", " ", "collectiveCorrelation", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"zOne", ",", " ", "zTwo"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
            "assumptions"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
      RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<independent: GHZ\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<independent: DFS candidate\>\"", ",", "\n", 
          "    ", "\"\<collective: GHZ\>\"", ",", 
          " ", "\"\<collective: DFS candidate\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
              "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "generators"}], ",", 
          "\n", "    ", "assumptions"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[43]:= ",
 CellID->1146801282,ExpressionUUID->"499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The four activities are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"8", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"8", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"32", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],
 ", respectively. Both coherences decay under independent noise, while the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{"01"},
      "Ket"], "+", 
     TemplateBox[{"10"},
      "Ket"]}], ")"}], "/", 
   SqrtBox["2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],
 " state is exactly stationary under collective dephasing. A protected \
subspace is useful for sensing only if the desired signal acts differently \
inside it; a signal proportional to the same collective ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],
 " operator would disappear there as well. Spatial correlations can therefore \
be either destructive or useful, depending on the signal geometry. See ",
 ButtonBox["Jeske, Cole, and Huelga",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1307.6301"], None}],
 " and ",
 ButtonBox["Hamann, Sekatski, and D\[UDoubleDot]r",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.13828"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->41202278,ExpressionUUID->"3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],

Cell["\<\
A negative Kossakowski eigenvalue would destroy complete positivity. Confirm \
that the helper rejects such an input:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1124146653,ExpressionUUID->"4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"correlatedDephasingGenerator", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ghzTwoQubitState", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"zOne", ",", " ", "zTwo"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[44]:= ",
 CellID->1232284935,ExpressionUUID->"7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<UnverifiedPhysicalCorrelationMatrix\>\"", ",", " ", "..."}], 
   "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],
 ", so an algebraically shaped but physically invalid noise matrix cannot \
enter unnoticed."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2082395230,ExpressionUUID->"11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],

Cell["\<\
Complex off-diagonal correlations are physical too when the matrix is \
Hermitian and positive semidefinite. Test the smallest such case:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2045146513,ExpressionUUID->"473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"complexCorrelation", ",", " ", "complexCorrelationGenerator"}], 
   "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"complexCorrelation", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"I", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "I"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"complexCorrelationGenerator", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"correlatedDephasingGenerator", "[", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"ghzTwoQubitState", ",", " ", "complexCorrelation", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"zOne", ",", " ", "zTwo"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<positive correlation eigenvalues\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"And", " ", "@@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", "complexCorrelation", "]"}], " ", ">=", 
       " ", "0"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<generator preserves Hermiticity\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    
    RowBox[{"complexCorrelationGenerator", " ", "==", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{
     "ConjugateTranspose", "[", "complexCorrelationGenerator", "]"}]}]}], ",",
    "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<generator preserves trace\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "complexCorrelationGenerator", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
     "0"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[45]:= ",
 CellID->25123057,ExpressionUUID->"12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All three entries are ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],
 ". The correlation matrix has eigenvalues ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43fcea2e-12ab-c026-7183-0388a75f930c"],
 ", and its complex phase does not spoil the generator's physical \
invariants."
}], "Text",
 CellID->371825621,ExpressionUUID->"5b416c07-c3d3-bf4f-097e-8660f6670595"],

Cell["Echo Control: Which Lost Phase Can Come Back?", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->1439628390,ExpressionUUID->"5add4728-e92e-eff1-0ae3-5f7588d8b5db"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Lindblad equation also draws a sharp boundary around quantum control. A \
constant or slowly varying detuning is a Hamiltonian error, and a ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"],
 " pulse can reverse its sign. Let the system evolve for half the total time, \
apply ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],
 ", and evolve for the other half."
}], "Text",
 CellID->497245720,ExpressionUUID->"7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],

Cell["\<\
Define free evolution under an arbitrary detuning and form the echo sequence:\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1090726268,ExpressionUUID->"4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"detuning", ",", " ", "echoUnitary"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"echoUnitary", " ", "=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"clockUnitary", "[", 
     RowBox[{"detuning", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"time", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "X", " ", ".", "\n",
     "   ", 
    RowBox[{"clockUnitary", "[", 
     RowBox[{"detuning", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"time", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[46]:= ",
 CellID->2124519200,ExpressionUUID->"494d6e39-7750-b6eb-7f72-806302ea1c31"],

Cell["Verify that the unknown static detuning cancels exactly:", "Text",
 CellID->617350884,ExpressionUUID->"39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"echoUnitary", " ", "==", " ", "X"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"detuning", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], 
     "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[47]:= ",
 CellID->1357963930,ExpressionUUID->"4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The echo returns the intended ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],
 " pulse independently of the unknown detuning. The same algebra creates an \
important sensing warning: if the desired signal is the static term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],
 ", the echo cancels that DC signal too."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1626918454,ExpressionUUID->"16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],

Cell["\<\
Verify the cancellation by replacing the unwanted detuning with the clock \
frequency:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->675379980,ExpressionUUID->"06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"echoUnitary", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"detuning", " ", "->", " ", "omega"}]}], ")"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    "X"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}], "]"}],
     " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[48]:= ",
 CellID->1331866192,ExpressionUUID->"05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],

Cell["\<\
Echo-assisted sensing must therefore distinguish signal from noise in some \
other way, for example through an AC signal synchronized with the pulse \
toggling. The same sign reversal also cannot undo ideal Markovian dephasing, \
because a dissipator is quadratic in its leak operator.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1391655620,ExpressionUUID->"583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that reversing the sign of the leak leaves the dissipator unchanged \
for a general qubit matrix:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->861714746,ExpressionUUID->"07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", "symbolicState"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"symbolicState", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"dissipator", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "Z"}], ",", " ", "symbolicState"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
   RowBox[{"dissipator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Z", ",", " ", "symbolicState"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[49]:= ",
 CellID->1192942815,ExpressionUUID->"503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is the control lesson: echo and dynamical decoupling can suppress \
static, slow, or spectrally structured phase noise, but they cannot refocus \
the constant-rate Markovian generator written here. In practice that \
distinction turns pulse design into noise spectroscopy, because the coherence \
under different pulse sequences reveals which frequencies the environment \
contains. See the filter-design treatment of ",
 ButtonBox["Biercuk, Doherty, and Uys",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1012.4262"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->556077107,ExpressionUUID->"60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],

Cell["\<\
Error-Corrected Sensing: Can We Remove the Noise but Keep the Signal?\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->15883883,ExpressionUUID->"40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "There is a deeper obstruction when the signal Hamiltonian and the dephasing \
act along the same axis. For the single Hermitian leak ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],
 ", the relevant Lindblad operator span is generated by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\|01d7d9"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],
 ". A signal proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],
 " lies inside that span; a signal proportional to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],
 " does not."
}], "Text",
 CellID->308842859,ExpressionUUID->"5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"],

Cell["\<\
Define a general matrix-span test with no physics-specific operator hidden \
inside it:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1108042358,ExpressionUUID->"73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "operatorSpanMemberQ", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"operatorSpanMemberQ", "[", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"operator_", "?", "MatrixQ"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"basis", " ", ":", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"___", "?", "MatrixQ"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"assumptions_", " ", ":", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}], " ", "/;", 
    "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"basis", " ", "===", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], " ", "||", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"SameQ", " ", "@@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"Dimensions", " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", 
          RowBox[{"basis", ",", " ", "operator"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
     ")"}]}], " ", ":=", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"coefficients", ",", " ", "membershipCondition"}], "}"}], ",", 
     "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"membershipCondition", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"If", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"basis", " ", "===", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"And", " ", "@@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", "operator", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], 
           "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"coefficients", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Unique", "[", "\"\<spanCoefficient\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
             " ", 
             RowBox[{"Length", "[", "basis", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", 
          "     ", 
          RowBox[{"With", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"variables", " ", "=", " ", "coefficients"}], "}"}], ",",
             "\n", "      ", 
            RowBox[{"Resolve", "[", "\n", "       ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Exists", "[", 
               RowBox[{"variables", ",", "\n", "        ", 
                RowBox[{"And", " ", "@@", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"Thread", "[", "\n", "          ", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"operator", " ", "-", "\n", "             ", 
                    RowBox[{"Total", "@", 
                    RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"coefficients", ",", " ", "basis"}], "}"}]}], 
                    "]"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}],
               ",", "\n", "       ", "Complexes"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
        "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Which", "[", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"TrueQ", "@", 
         RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"Implies", "[", 
           RowBox[{"assumptions", ",", " ", "membershipCondition"}], "]"}], 
          "]"}]}], ",", " ", "True", ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{"TrueQ", "@", 
         RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"Implies", "[", 
           RowBox[{"assumptions", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Not", "[", "membershipCondition", "]"}]}], "]"}], 
          "]"}]}], ",", " ", "False", ",", "\n", "    ", "True", ",", "\n", 
        "    ", 
        RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<AssumptionDependentSpanMembership\>\"", ",", "\n", 
          "     ", 
          RowBox[{"<|", 
           RowBox[{
            
            RowBox[{"\"\<MembershipCondition\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
             "membershipCondition"}], ",", "\n", "       ", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<Assumptions\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "assumptions"}]}], 
           "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"operatorSpanMemberQ", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"operator_", "?", "MatrixQ"}], ",", " ", "basis_List", ",", " ", 
     
     RowBox[{"assumptions_", " ", ":", " ", "True"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<IncompatibleMatrixBasis\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<OperatorDimensions\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "operator", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<BasisDimensions\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"Dimensions", " ", "/@", " ", "basis"}], ")"}]}]}], "|>"}]}],
     "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"operatorSpanMemberQ", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n",
    "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidOperatorSpanInput\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[50]:= ",
 CellID->1009200201,ExpressionUUID->"69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],

Cell["\<\
Test parallel and transverse signals against the dephasing span:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->752465254,ExpressionUUID->"409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "spanAmplitude", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<parallel signal Z\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"operatorSpanMemberQ", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Z", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"id2", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<transverse signal X\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"operatorSpanMemberQ", "[", 
     RowBox[{"X", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"id2", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<assumption-dependent span\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"operatorSpanMemberQ", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Z", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"spanAmplitude", " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<nonzero span amplitude\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"operatorSpanMemberQ", "[", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"Z", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"spanAmplitude", " ", "Z"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"spanAmplitude", " ", "!=", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<malformed operator\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"operatorSpanMemberQ", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"id2", ",", " ", "Z"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[51]:= ",
 CellID->891183881,ExpressionUUID->"10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first two entries are ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["False"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d45428e-8fa1-6801-4b7b-5be82a543b6b"],
 ". Without an assumption on its coefficient, the symbolic span returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<AssumptionDependentSpanMembership\>\"", ",", " ", "..."}], 
   "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "604bb87d-3174-a116-1048-32274006f07c"],
 "; declaring the coefficient nonzero makes the membership ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "763191a2-6f8b-197a-1fce-080c0a3e6840"],
 ". The malformed vector also returns a named ",
 Cell[BoxData["Failure"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "635fdfdb-2856-deda-1164-d68549e0a420"],
 ". The parallel signal is algebraically indistinguishable from the noise \
generators, while the transverse signal contributes a new direction. In other \
words, a code that removes every unknown ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f6eb37a-d9e9-6713-3515-2b27df9c4a79"],
 " phase will also remove the desired ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8469dd-bfc7-2a7a-04bb-80873a727940"],
 " phase unless extra structure makes them distinguishable."
}], "Text",
 CellID->741634648,ExpressionUUID->"182ee0c1-720e-fc83-49d5-f9ab07b8c6e9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This small rank calculation is the one-qubit shadow of a general result: \
with fast control and noiseless ancillas, error-corrected Heisenberg scaling \
under Markovian noise is possible precisely when the signal Hamiltonian has a \
component outside the Lindblad span. See ",
 ButtonBox["Zhou, Zhang, Preskill, and Jiang",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.02445"], None}],
 ". The orientation of the sensor is therefore part of the error-correction \
design, not an afterthought."
}], "Text",
 CellID->359589406,ExpressionUUID->"3921e4bb-f5e4-3596-68de-fde483969ffc"],

Cell["\<\
The Discarded Environment: Where Did the Phase Information Go?\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->533832725,ExpressionUUID->"13db9173-5387-1c16-41f8-093d6632677c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The master equation is unconditional: it describes the state after the \
environmental record has been ignored. The phase-flip representation computed \
above makes this concrete. Each realization can be viewed as a unitary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6804c0ab-fd16-b7db-183b-d9f4f4a01d21"],
 " error with a classical label, but averaging over an inaccessible label \
produces a mixed state. For a single qubit, even dephasing caused by a \
quantum bath can be reproduced by classical random-unitary noise at the level \
of reduced dynamics; see ",
 ButtonBox["Crow and Joynt",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.6383"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->739917449,ExpressionUUID->"77076ae4-09e5-8344-1d3c-83ceaf91d1ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This observation changes the recovery question. System-only control cannot \
infer which random phase occurred, and the Lindblad-span obstruction applies \
under that access model. If the environment is monitored with unit efficiency \
and the record identifies the phase kicks, conditional feedback can recover \
information that the unconditional density matrix has lost. Ideal continuous \
monitoring can restore the noiseless frequency QFI for parallel Markovian \
dephasing; see ",
 ButtonBox["Albarelli et al.",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.05891"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->473762610,ExpressionUUID->"4289b0c6-8043-1b93-72b6-29a031f669f9"],

Cell["\<\
In other words, \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]dephasing destroyed the phase\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] is too strong. At finite time the reduced state \
retains the nonzero frequency information computed above, while dephasing \
transfers part of that information out of the reduced state. The master \
equation alone does not determine whether the missing part remains \
recoverable from an environmental record.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1751712322,ExpressionUUID->"070f3e08-556d-9d60-2d34-b0525c19e44a"],

Cell["\<\
Beyond the Semigroup: Replace the Exponential by a Coherence Function\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->1390140890,ExpressionUUID->"6d593b15-c37a-9c59-1b66-b35ef60ce6a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The constant rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4140e475-1e41-1f16-777f-fe3f9bf4627c"],
 " is a physical hypothesis, not merely a convenient parameter. A time-local \
pure-dephasing equation"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1031105928,ExpressionUUID->"67f13035-938c-831a-0d8e-aa7f263eee60"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "."], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "/", "2"}], ",", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1410588720,ExpressionUUID->"16b44e14-0404-e868-3e4c-605eadb6bab2"],

Cell["has coherence factor", "Text",
 CellID->1051974278,ExpressionUUID->"70bc3c38-1a7f-2cd8-2043-b6629f0a7622"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
    StyleBox["exp",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "[", 
    RowBox[{"-", "2", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], "]"}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1989924844,ExpressionUUID->"7e10bd94-ae42-3b4d-262f-34d1cbf48997"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every result above that depends only on transverse contrast survives after \
replacing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5fdf5ac0-01aa-1326-05e5-53aab05f7e0c"],
 " by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "013c2307-fb8b-27c7-30c3-bb60fe3f8d2d"],
 ". In other words, one function carries the entire temporal structure of \
pure dephasing."
}], "Text",
 CellID->695529426,ExpressionUUID->"4b734859-75e7-efa6-7901-62030393b58c"],

Cell["Build that function for an arbitrary time-local rate:", "Text",
 CellID->767788723,ExpressionUUID->"4ae31c17-eefa-a706-7a90-96508a8c0a6c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"coherenceFactor", ",", " ", "rateTime"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"coherenceFactor", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"rateFunction", " ", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"_Function", " ", "|", " ", "_Symbol"}], ")"}]}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"time_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"coherenceFactor", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rateFunction", ",", " ", "time", ",", " ", "True"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"coherenceFactor", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"rateFunction", " ", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"_Function", " ", "|", " ", "_Symbol"}], ")"}]}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"time_", "?", "nonnegativeParameterQ"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions_", "?", "scalarExpressionQ"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", "\n", "      ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"rateFunction", "[", "rateTime", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"rateTime", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", 
         "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", "assumptions"}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", "assumptions"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"coherenceFactor", "[", "arguments___", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", 
   "  ", 
   RowBox[{"Failure", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<InvalidRateFunction\>\"", ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Arguments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"HoldForm", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", "arguments", "}"}], "]"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[52]:= ",
 CellID->494419947,ExpressionUUID->"00844d77-2817-3ec6-30bc-653149a3842c"],

Cell["\<\
Compare a constant rate with a rate that grows linearly at short times:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1581507689,ExpressionUUID->"20b97f64-b973-0c8a-5047-774e380656d0"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"kappa", ",", " ", "coherenceExamples"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"coherenceExamples", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"assumptions", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"gamma", ",", " ", "kappa", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", 
         " ", "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"gamma", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{"kappa", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"<|", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<constant rate\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"coherenceFactor", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
          RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "gamma"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "time", ",", " ",
          "assumptions"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<linear short-time rate\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"coherenceFactor", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
          RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"kappa", " ", "s"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "time", ",", " ", 
         "assumptions"}], "]"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[53]:= ",
 CellID->2120100675,ExpressionUUID->"04469009-6b02-dcc3-2c7d-0a530eb4a629"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The semigroup gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "2", 
     StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e35d333-5bd5-ef26-77ca-cb7d5e61b20c"],
 ", while the linearly rising rate gives the Gaussian short-time law ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["\[Kappa]", "TI"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5547dfb6-0e84-e145-037c-d6f0ab36b3af"],
 ". The latter is the generic shape expected before a finite-bandwidth \
environment has forgotten its initial correlations."
}], "Text",
 CellID->950326543,ExpressionUUID->"12b61bfc-9cd7-eca9-424d-92a61563b6f3"],

Cell["\<\
Now keep the contrast symbolic and recompute the frequency information:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1689126594,ExpressionUUID->"451364b5-819d-fb99-7321-7dff3029c9e3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "contrast", ",", " ", "generalClockVector", ",", " ", "generalClockQFI"}], 
   "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"generalClockVector", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"contrast", "[", "time", "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
       RowBox[{"omega", " ", "time"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"contrast", "[", "time", "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"omega", " ", "time"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"generalClockQFI", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Map", "[", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"TrigFactor", ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"<|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<radial term\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{"generalClockVector", " ", ".", " ", 
          RowBox[{"D", "[", 
           RowBox[{"generalClockVector", ",", " ", "omega"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
        "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<frequency QFI\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "      ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"D", "[", 
           RowBox[{"generalClockVector", ",", " ", "omega"}], "]"}], " ", ".",
           "\n", "       ", 
          RowBox[{"D", "[", 
           RowBox[{"generalClockVector", ",", " ", "omega"}], "]"}]}]}]}], 
       "|>"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"omega", ",", " ", "time", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"contrast", "[", "time", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
       RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", 
        RowBox[{"contrast", "[", "time", "]"}], " ", "<", " ", "1"}]}]}], 
     "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[54]:= ",
 CellID->1490757098,ExpressionUUID->"13b49e24-0fb7-4441-414b-178eaa422eab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The output gives a zero radial term and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "445bf28f-7a5a-ecd1-6c78-ebe97fecb63b"],
 ". Consequently, the metrological optimum and the many-probe scaling are \
controlled by the short-time behavior of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "089aa42d-ce49-3603-38b9-3e76ebfd9d69"],
 ", not by the word \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]non-Markovian\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] alone. Finite-bandwidth dephasing can restore an \
entanglement advantage absent in the semigroup model; see ",
 ButtonBox["Chin, Huelga, and Plenio",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1103.1219"], None}],
 ". More generally, the violation of the short-time semigroup law is the \
decisive feature identified by ",
 ButtonBox["Smirne et al.",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1511.02708"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->148290444,ExpressionUUID->"48fccab3-b886-a0f7-7883-e3fd3930f2dd"],

Cell["The Rate Must Be Physical: Where the Model Fails", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->1707667820,ExpressionUUID->"0cdaad60-2181-5e26-34f9-454a5034250c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The condition ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "542cff75-84e0-b601-7dd3-f73f2c9a1d6b"],
 " is not decorative. A negative constant rate would make the transverse \
Bloch vector grow beyond the sphere and turn a valid density matrix into a \
matrix with a negative eigenvalue. That would be a negative probability, so \
it cannot describe a completely positive Markovian evolution."
}], "Text",
 CellID->933399197,ExpressionUUID->"00dd9d4d-f7ec-565f-30e2-151681993ca5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The helper ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"dephasingLeak", "[", "gamma", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0d66b502-775d-ec4c-3b1d-2d6c02e9b696"],
 " represents a Lindblad rate through the amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a3bfee8-9a0e-4a4b-6bd8-f7b21fbb1891"],
 " and rejects a negative numeric argument. Even if a negative number were \
inserted directly under the square root, it would only attach a phase to the \
leak, and a dissipator is unchanged by such a phase. To test the forbidden \
generator coefficient, continue the symbolic solution itself from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "333832e2-8bec-4128-62c7-abcc2d991072"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["g", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78cf51d6-d7cd-4672-28f5-4893e2782d58"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->955179929,ExpressionUUID->"1d9e3d6f-99f1-7c1e-4ba5-b5491f844764"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Test the determinant of an initially pure equatorial state under the \
formally continued rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["g", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "710db4a8-d877-0db2-2732-2df5d9025798"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->775067320,ExpressionUUID->"71e12f72-3ad4-a92f-279e-c73cbf66f875"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "positiveRate", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Det", "[", 
     RowBox[{"blochState", " ", "@@", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"clockSolution", " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Join", "[", "\n", "       ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"x0", ",", " ", "y0", ",", " ", "z0"}], "}"}], " ", "->",
             "\n", "         ", 
            RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
             RowBox[{"clockExample", "[", "\"\<ProbeState\>\"", "]"}], 
             "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "       ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"omega", " ", "->", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"gamma", " ", "->", " ", 
             RowBox[{"-", "positiveRate"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], 
     "]"}], " ", "<", " ", "0"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"positiveRate", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "Reals"}],
      "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"positiveRate", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
    RowBox[{"time", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[55]:= ",
 CellID->72268088,ExpressionUUID->"06ea8612-dd18-b4f0-2ee9-185fd4921eda"],

Cell["\<\
The state immediately leaves the Bloch ball. A time-dependent rate may be \
negative over a finite interval only if the accumulated rate remains physical:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->546416532,ExpressionUUID->"0b02f270-2101-5c3d-3931-f43a50b42707"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "0", "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"for", "\[NonBreakingSpace]", "every", "\[NonBreakingSpace]"}],
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "0"}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->2117784656,ExpressionUUID->"2d1868bf-f524-2aaf-5b27-81f8fcd178f5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "equivalently ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "\[LessEqual]", "1"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "669caa83-24d6-d7e9-0ea3-43ed4d60bd33"],
 ". A physical negative interval makes ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ae50fd0-6d1f-8fa4-0a9a-a69a04abd58e"],
 " increase and marks a failure of CP divisibility, but it cannot be replaced \
by a negative constant starting at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66e7a4a8-d710-64fe-0e9c-3df5e2a54ec4"],
 ". The distinction between divisibility and information backflow is reviewed \
by ",
 ButtonBox["Rivas, Huelga, and Plenio",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1405.0303"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->853117843,ExpressionUUID->"3e73fafe-05d0-7203-6600-f3b8ac654169"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Exhibit the distinction with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fb7b09a-ac3b-ef52-254c-29c7c5cfb5b8"],
 ". Its integral from zero is never negative, although its instantaneous \
value becomes negative:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->623836386,ExpressionUUID->"12c044c4-b778-74e1-42f0-5da1c20d5ecb"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "rateAmplitude", ",", " ", "oscillatoryRate", ",", " ", 
    "physicalNegativeRateExample"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"oscillatoryRate", "[", "rateTime_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"rateAmplitude", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "rateTime", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"physicalNegativeRateExample", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"<|", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<rate at 3 Pi/2\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"oscillatoryRate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"3", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<accumulated rate\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"Integrate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"oscillatoryRate", "[", "rateTime", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"rateTime", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}]}], 
        "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<coherence growth at 3 Pi/2\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"D", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"coherenceFactor", "[", "\n", "        ", 
            RowBox[{"oscillatoryRate", ",", " ", "time", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"rateAmplitude", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
              RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
           "       ", "time"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
         RowBox[{"time", " ", "->", " ", 
          RowBox[{"3", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}]}]}]}], ")"}]}]}], "|>"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
    
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Element", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"rateAmplitude", ",", " ", "time"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       "Reals"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"rateAmplitude", " ", ">", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[56]:= ",
 CellID->564394165,ExpressionUUID->"3d9aa029-60a8-273a-6bb9-3a7311428a00"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The outputs are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64adc082-4122-deff-0c52-d9ec70d4a4c5"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e451771-8a55-ceec-267a-8f3b2fe19436"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "2", 
     StyleBox["a", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4670f053-f537-0b3f-6e0f-ea1cfcc25605"],
 ". The family is completely positive from its initial time because the \
accumulated rate stays nonnegative, but the coherence grows during part of \
the evolution, so the intermediate maps are not CP divisible."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2048244887,ExpressionUUID->"330aabc0-bdd5-22a3-6109-42aa34607089"],

Cell["\<\
Finally, probe the reusable interfaces with tensor-valued scalars, negative \
physical parameters, nonphysical Ramsey matrices, and malformed assumptions:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1432457359,ExpressionUUID->"38c8cb12-19a5-fbf9-68f7-e35c9851c9c3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"<|", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\"\<nested Bloch entry rejected\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"FailureQ", "@", 
     RowBox[{"clockBloch", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
       " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<vector rate rejected\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"FailureQ", "@", 
     RowBox[{"phaseFlipChannel", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"id2", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
   "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<negative channel rate rejected\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"FailureQ", "@", 
     RowBox[{"clockChannel", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"id2", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<nonphysical Ramsey input rejected\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", 
    "   ", 
    RowBox[{"FailureQ", "@", 
     RowBox[{"ramseyProbability", "[", "\n", "     ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "1", ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "5"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<nested QFI entry rejected\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"FailureQ", "@", 
     RowBox[{"blochFisherInformation", "[", "\n", "     ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
       " ", "omega", ",", " ", "\"\<Mixed\>\""}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   
   RowBox[{"\"\<nested QFI-matrix entry rejected\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"FailureQ", "@", 
     RowBox[{"blochFisherInformationMatrix", "[", "\n", "     ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "omega", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<vector time rejected\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"FailureQ", "@", 
     RowBox[{"coherenceFactor", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<malformed assumptions rejected\>\"", " ", "->", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"FailureQ", "@", 
     RowBox[{"coherenceFactor", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Sin", ",", " ", "time", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"time", " ", ">=", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], 
  "|>"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[57]:= ",
 CellID->200346680,ExpressionUUID->"70d705b8-410a-1477-20ec-9ce270bf7f5d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every entry is ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "737c509e-bc52-eefb-2104-49d835e4b4c1"],
 ". Symbolic scalar parameters remain available for derivation, while \
explicitly nonphysical numeric inputs are routed to structured failures \
before matrix algebra begins."
}], "Text",
 CellID->447384324,ExpressionUUID->"01a44b6b-c85f-9e0e-375c-6334e9ebe554"],

Cell["\<\
The monotone exponential is therefore not only a solution; it is the physical \
hypothesis that the bath has no resolved memory on the probe's timescale.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1438124241,ExpressionUUID->"10bcaec6-cc03-bcfd-4043-47a3e5b706c7"],

Cell["\<\
Before leaving the clock, let us summarize the most important points we have \
computed:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2000382747,ExpressionUUID->"25120901-cfbc-a8e6-5321-a16aea4efacc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A commuting Hamiltonian turns the transverse Bloch vector while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3ee7491f-72c3-8814-669d-61590777db7e"],
 " shrinks it, and neither changes the energy populations."
}], "Item",
 CellID->902867877,ExpressionUUID->"67860241-8011-89c8-0dbd-a42b31a5db12"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Except at the completely switched-off corner, the fixed-point algebra is \
generated by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "\|01d7d9"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1318f44b-7a0d-b86f-4127-ee157fb90ab5"],
 ", while the coherence modes have Liouvillian eigenvalues ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[PlusMinus]", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "221ecbfd-1ed7-d323-5225-e2a79b63be09"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1315202099,ExpressionUUID->"3f067a83-888f-4db3-653e-73ed293a1799"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The same evolution is an ideal ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "287fc527-5526-9e30-5804-dc815cd0e51a"],
 " rotation followed by a stochastic phase-flip channel, which connects ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2207e002-80f7-0285-523c-fa6c308250ef"],
 " directly to computational error."
}], "Item",
 CellID->376763343,ExpressionUUID->"440467ae-8db5-79b4-6c3c-7e0824404b9e"],

Cell["\<\
The Ramsey probability is an oscillation whose visibility decays as the clock \
loses coherence.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->126027414,ExpressionUUID->"141585f4-d1c1-5bbd-3c2a-1cb1e0742987"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The state carries distinct local information about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d27d006-86b8-9131-64dc-ca603332e01b"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e44340b-ef5c-51d5-667b-ae548ae9233f"],
 ", with a diagonal two-parameter QFI matrix for the equatorial probe."
}], "Item",
 CellID->570920987,ExpressionUUID->"321034f4-436e-dcec-622f-adbe7618a636"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the ideal repeated-interrogation model, the unconstrained optimum is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "*"], "=", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1287d3f9-6500-de4e-42bc-caa30cbaa494"],
 " and the feasible optimum is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["min",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "{", 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "*"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3035d7f6-28ea-dcd5-61ca-ceb0489ca63f"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->378517449,ExpressionUUID->"087f5f2f-6486-1b59-3805-56890d3369a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With enough total time to reach both optima, independent Markovian \
dephasing makes a GHZ clock gain phase ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ddf1aac-cdaa-cd7e-2be4-9309e45c9444"],
 " times faster and require readout ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b41c4a9-15e8-1804-597e-ddf3a39d6b6e"],
 " times sooner, leaving the asymptotic optimized scaling unchanged."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1671903560,ExpressionUUID->"13ecd9ee-6506-67bb-4193-d0c80cb34d81"],

Cell["\<\
Spatially collective dephasing protects a two-qubit decoherence-free state \
that independent dephasing destroys.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->1307059254,ExpressionUUID->"6724c974-bdf1-27a5-0edb-e13e3b858d8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A spin echo cancels static Hamiltonian detuning and any indistinguishable \
static signal, but it cannot cancel the Markovian dissipator because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "\|01d49f", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b52875c-0948-9ae8-5961-1f06a8e2e832"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->538512558,ExpressionUUID->"53412643-5a68-df00-017e-b82d5f02a26a"],

Cell["\<\
Error correction can preserve a signal only when that signal is \
distinguishable from the Lindblad noise directions.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->824717693,ExpressionUUID->"696f5b1d-d56b-3a26-1f15-5346dc1f890c"],

Cell["\<\
Monitoring the environment changes what can be recovered because the \
unconditional state has discarded the error record.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->496527141,ExpressionUUID->"0eb02373-2484-618c-364f-bb3d4d3133d6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Replacing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640353f1-ff8e-e9b3-0c31-4abafa38bb99"],
 " by a general contrast ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37161f66-4600-a3a8-5d2d-974073baf1f2"],
 " gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e44757e-c407-f813-567c-6d3bedb3cb79"],
 " and exposes the short-time semigroup assumption."
}], "Item",
 CellID->2009363188,ExpressionUUID->"07a61755-6475-fbf7-2d5d-8f1f0d01c9dd"],

Cell["\<\
A negative constant dephasing rate violates positivity, while a physical \
time-dependent negative interval must obey the accumulated-rate condition.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->55669068,ExpressionUUID->"539b0e4e-9e5a-5525-01b8-a0281bef3c0f"],

Cell["Research Questions: What Should We Ask Next?", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->1753574084,ExpressionUUID->"1cd82739-42e3-b7ed-44e7-bf6376971d37"],

Cell["\<\
The master equation is simple enough to solve exactly and rich enough to \
organize a serious research program. The most important next questions are \
these:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2038359728,ExpressionUUID->"0971a20b-7913-467e-3f0e-445578a62d44"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Foundational: what microscopic environment produces ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,
  FontWeight->"Bold",ExpressionUUID->"09df342d-d743-5809-3fe4-ae76e2f62b53"],
 StyleBox["?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Start from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"S", "B"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   StyleBox["B", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a0cc1e9-e2ca-26d9-3a33-d8b2977c8c23"],
 " and derive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21fdaace-430e-f3f9-5782-43a876b8c1c3"],
 " from a spectral density, temperature, coupling strength, and initial \
system-environment state. Then identify the timescale on which ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b4e2dea-4a49-bf2e-4975-c4b46ffd0274"],
 " becomes exponential."
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellID->1525364821,ExpressionUUID->"10b057f0-cb39-4e6e-4040-4ebdeecc14b4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Application: can one infer the environment from probe data?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Estimate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41c6bfc6-0792-5005-77fd-36a0b227236f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62752e4e-571f-d961-120a-c02862aba84b"],
 " jointly, resolve the nonregular ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", 
   SuperscriptBox["0", "+"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34ee5221-bb14-cc46-5c96-4b8b3ea696ac"],
 " boundary, test SLD compatibility or the Holevo bound, compare exponential, \
Gaussian, and telegraph-noise likelihoods, and design Ramsey or echo \
sequences that distinguish their spectra."
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellID->1535108406,ExpressionUUID->"166277e1-e8de-815f-3e12-6eca8968d3a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Foundational: where is the lost information stored?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Compare the unconditional state with monitored quantum trajectories. \
Determine how detector efficiency limits environment-assisted correction and \
metrological recovery."
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellID->1528788962,ExpressionUUID->"0ae7a534-7379-468c-3a9c-3d7e060c2cd6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Both: which spatial noise modes matter?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Replace two probes by a network with correlation matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["C", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34baef30-7963-b757-5c59-077a78171dbd"],
 ". Search for decoherence-free or approximately protected subspaces whose \
signal response is not removed with the noise."
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellID->1505774531,ExpressionUUID->"15ce0314-20ee-2b64-43f5-9b5e509b764e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Application: which entangled states are optimal at finite \
resources?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Move beyond the product-versus-GHZ comparison to spin-squeezed, partially \
entangled, and code states, including preparation time and measurement \
restrictions."
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellID->535490749,ExpressionUUID->"38a9ac88-4644-6c0e-6856-45d273f13754"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Application: when does a Ramsey probe become a clock?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Add a noisy local oscillator, cyclic operation, phase unwrapping, \
feedback, and dead time. Optimize Allan stability rather than one-shot QFI."
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellID->1238905205,ExpressionUUID->"64802aa2-b136-451c-0cbf-c30fc0c32c66"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Foundational: what is the thermodynamic cost of losing a phase \
reference?",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Track system, bath, and interaction energies together with entropy \
production. Constant system energy does not settle that question."
}], "ItemNumbered",
 CellID->2125008310,ExpressionUUID->"67771ff6-ea2e-a98b-0d0c-96b38fd8fbd1"],

Cell["\<\
These questions are not decorations added after the calculation. Each one is \
forced by an assumption we used: constant rate, discarded environment, \
independent probes, unrestricted measurements, or an ideal external phase \
reference.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1684656716,ExpressionUUID->"233ecb8e-17f3-8d32-52c5-e2e8a187d418"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us (and What Comes Next)", "Subsubsection",
 CellID->2057792111,ExpressionUUID->"7dd949a9-d8cf-50b3-2be7-60f2d97a2299"],

Cell["\<\
We began with a Hamiltonian that writes a useful phase and an environment \
that hides it from the reduced state, then turned that competition into a \
Bloch trajectory, a fixed-point algebra, a computational phase-flip channel, \
a Ramsey fringe, a joint-estimation problem, an optimal sensing time, an \
entanglement limit, a spatial-correlation test, a control boundary, and an \
error-correction criterion. The constant-rate master equation now says \
exactly what an ideal Ramsey probe can learn and exactly which questions it \
cannot answer without a microscopic bath, an environmental record, a \
multi-probe noise geometry, or a complete clock loop.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->408837332,ExpressionUUID->"4a74bc9f-39f4-5114-7a0b-35d9bf81207e"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (February 17, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"598f41e5-f1df-a461-0fb5-58ce806b0f4b"
]
